# Agents and structured output — the headline, 65.6 t/s (4.7x bare decode).
#
# The headline configuration: a Qwen3.8-27B ROCmFP4-FAST target with an FP4
# DFlash2 sidecar, drafts sized from measured acceptance.
#
#   Radeon 8060S, greedy, 300 tokens, structured output:
#   bare decode      14.0 t/s
#   fixed draft n=3  41.6
#   fixed draft n=7  20.2      <- the same ceiling, without adaptive sizing
#   this preset      65.6 t/s   (4.7x bare)
#
# Adaptive is what makes n-max safe. Fixed n=7 collapses to 18% draft
# acceptance on this pair; adaptive holds 96% while drafting longer. n-max is
# a ceiling here, not a tuning parameter.
#
# On prose this reads 26.1 t/s rather than 65.6. Content dominates
# configuration — identical weights at identical context differ by 2.5x purely
# on whether the output is predictable.
#
# The 65.6 figure was taken on a short high-power burst (79 C, 115 W) that this
# chassis cannot sustain. On the everyday power profile the same configuration
# reads 55.0 t/s. Both are real; which one you get is a thermal question.
#
# REQUIRES a Qwen3.8-27B target — the sidecar is trained against it. For another
# family, repoint LLAMA_ARG_SPEC_DRAFT_HF_REPO at that model's own DFlash2
# sidecar. A mismatched sidecar does not merely run slower: it drafts tokens the
# target rejects, and you pay the full draft cost for nothing.
LLAMA_ARG_N_GPU_LAYERS=999
LLAMA_ARG_FLASH_ATTN=on
LLAMA_ARG_CTX_SIZE=32768
LLAMA_ARG_UBATCH=512
LLAMA_ARG_BATCH=2048
LLAMA_ARG_JINJA=1

LLAMA_ARG_SPEC_TYPE=draft-dflash
LLAMA_ARG_SPEC_DRAFT_HF_REPO=agentionai/Qwen3.8-27B-DFlash2-ROCmFP4-FAST-GGUF
LLAMA_ARG_N_GPU_LAYERS_DRAFT=99

LLAMA_ARG_SPEC_DRAFT_ADAPTIVE=1
LLAMA_ARG_SPEC_DRAFT_N_MIN=3
LLAMA_ARG_SPEC_DRAFT_N_MAX=7
